  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Consider the unit circle from Question 13: $x^2+y^2=1$, with centre $O$ at the origin and $A(1,0)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q10-a",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let the point $T$ be in the first quadrant with a $y$-coordinate of $\\frac13$. Find the exact value of",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p14-q10-a-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "the $x$-coordinate of point $T$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{3}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=1-\\left(\\frac13\\right)^2\\\\x^2&=\\frac89\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{3}\\end{align*}$$Take the positive root because $T$ is in quadrant I.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 20
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q10-a-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "$\\cos(180^\\circ-\\angle TOA)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{3}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos(180^\\circ-\\angle TOA)&=-\\cos(\\angle TOA)\\\\\\cos(180^\\circ-\\angle TOA)&=-\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{3}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 16
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q10-a-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "$\\tan(180^\\circ-\\angle TOA)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-\\frac{\\sqrt2}{4}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan(180^\\circ-\\angle TOA)&=-\\tan(\\angle TOA)\\\\\\tan(180^\\circ-\\angle TOA)&=-\\frac{1/3}{2\\sqrt2/3}\\\\\\tan(180^\\circ-\\angle TOA)&=-\\frac1{2\\sqrt2}\\\\\\tan(180^\\circ-\\angle TOA)&=-\\frac{\\sqrt2}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 21
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q10-a-iv",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iv",
            "prompt": "$\\tan(180^\\circ+\\angle TOA)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{\\sqrt2}{4}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan(180^\\circ+\\angle TOA)&=\\tan(\\angle TOA)\\\\\\tan(180^\\circ+\\angle TOA)&=\\frac{1/3}{2\\sqrt2/3}\\\\\\tan(180^\\circ+\\angle TOA)&=\\frac1{2\\sqrt2}\\\\\\tan(180^\\circ+\\angle TOA)&=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 21
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q10-b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Let the point $W$ be in the second quadrant with a $y$-coordinate of $\\frac1{\\sqrt2}$. Find the exact value of",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p14-q10-b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "the $x$-coordinate of $W$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=1-\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\right)^2\\\\x^2&=\\frac12\\\\x&=-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\end{align*}$$Take the negative root because $W$ is in quadrant II.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 20
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q10-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "$\\angle WOA$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$135^\\circ$",
              "worked": "The coordinate magnitudes are equal, so the reference angle is $45^\\circ$. Since $W$ is in quadrant II,\n$$\\angle WOA=180^\\circ-45^\\circ=135^\\circ.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 14
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q10-b-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "$\\sin(\\angle WOA)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac1{\\sqrt2}$",
              "worked": "On the unit circle, sine is the $y$-coordinate, so $\\sin(\\angle WOA)=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p14-q10-b-iv",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iv",
            "prompt": "$\\cos(\\angle WOA)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}$",
              "worked": "On the unit circle, cosine is the $x$-coordinate, so $\\cos(\\angle WOA)=-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
